note as DEP_diagram_01_iam
  Connects to other modules via:
  audit_log, clinical_access_grants, data_access_log, dsar_requests,
  tenant_memberships, tracked_subjects, user_permission_grants,
  user_profiles, user_role_assignments, users_history
end note

note as REC_SECURITY_EVENTS_diagram_01_iam
  REC 3.7 — SCOPE OF security_events
security_events is authentication/session-specific (login, MFA, token,
lockout). The platform-wide, tamper-evident activity trail lives in
audit.audit_log. Both are append-only; they are complementary, not
duplicates. Correlate via user_id + recorded_at when reconstructing a
security timeline.
end note

note as ACCOUNT_PERSON_BOUNDARY
  ACCOUNT/PERSON BOUNDARY
  iam.users is an authentication account. profiles.persons is the human identity.
  profiles.person_account_links is optional and versioned. Never require a login
  account to create a patient, newborn, emergency record, deceased person or
  external practitioner. Authorization is evaluated on the account plus the
  currently selected person/profile/tenant context.
end note


